{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context (DONE -- see ticket comments for full receipts)\nCut fix release 0.13.1 from reviewed main per docs/releasing.md, following on from\n0.13.0/v0.13.0. Known risk carried in from ticket hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo (0.13.0\nclosed FAILED): the mcp_registry job failed post-publish there (description length),\nPyPI immutability blocked re-dispatch, and the manual mcp-publisher fallback was blocked by\na navapbc org OAuth-App restriction, leaving the registry reporting 0.12.0 as isLatest.\n\nRESULT: this release did not hit that failure mode -- release.yml run 33290369748 completed\nevery job successfully, including mcp_registry (registry now reports 0.13.1 as isLatest,\nstatus=active). No exception needed; no follow-up ticket required for this risk.\n\n## Plan (executed -- see ticket comments for full receipts)\nWorktree from origin/main -> version bump (pyproject.toml, server.json, uv.lock) ->\nCHANGELOG curation -> api_surface_baseline regen -> preflight (version-lockstep guard,\nrelease tests, lint, typecheck, full test suite, build, twine check) -> commit (DCO +\nChange-Id + rebar-ticket trailer) -> Gerrit change 2407 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0\nunresolved comments) -> Submit (merged as 5ae9eb72b86b on main) -> release.yml dispatched\nwith version=0.13.1 (run 33290369748) -> pypi environment approved -> all jobs succeeded ->\nverified PyPI/PEP 740/GitHub Release/MCP Registry/Homebrew -> channel install +\nscripts/probe_rebar.py (142 passed, 0 failed) -> receipts recorded -> closing.\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml -- package version bump\n- server.json -- MCP manifest/package version bump\n- uv.lock -- root package version lockstep with pyproject.toml\n- CHANGELOG.md -- new 0.13.1 release section and compare links\n- tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json -- __version__ bump\n\n## Rollback / failure policy (not invoked -- release succeeded cleanly)\nPolicy was: yank + bump-forward on any post-publish failure, never overwrite/retag; accept\na documented [non-codebase, known-blocked] exception only for a repeat mcp_registry failure.\nNot needed -- every job, including mcp_registry, succeeded on the first release.yml run.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the version-lockstep release guard script against pyproject.toml and server.json with\n  version 0.13.1 and confirm it exits 0.\n- Run \"make lint\", \"make typecheck\", and \"make test\" under the worktree virtualenv and\n  confirm each exits 0.\n- Run \"python -m build\" to produce the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist, then \"python -m twine check\"\n  against the built artifacts and confirm it exits 0.\n- Run the pypi-attestations verifier against the published 0.13.1 wheel, scoped to the\n  navapbc/rebar repository, and confirm it exits 0.\n- Install the channel-published nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 build and run the packaged\n  scripts/probe_rebar.py probe against it, confirming zero failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] pyproject.toml declares version 0.13.1.\n- [x] server.json top-level version is 0.13.1.\n- [x] Every server.json packages[].version is 0.13.1.\n- [x] uv.lock records the root nava-rebar package at version 0.13.1.\n- [x] Running \"uv lock --check\" exits 0.\n- [x] CHANGELOG.md contains a 0.13.1 section dated with today's release date.\n- [x] CHANGELOG.md has a fresh Unreleased section and correct 0.13.1 compare links.\n- [x] tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json reflects __version__ 0.13.1.\n- [x] The release_guards.py version-lockstep check exits 0 for version 0.13.1 against\n      pyproject.toml and server.json.\n- [x] The release-specific guard and workflow pin unit tests\n      (tests/unit/test_release_guards.py and tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py) all pass.\n- [x] \"make lint\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [x] \"make typecheck\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [x] \"make test\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [x] \"python -m build\" produces the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist.\n- [x] \"python -m twine check\" exits 0 for the built artifacts.\n- [x] The release commit contains DCO sign-off, a Gerrit Change-Id, and this rebar-ticket\n      trailer.\n- [x] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 on the release change.\n- [x] Gerrit records Verified +1 on the release change.\n- [x] Gerrit has no unresolved comments on the release change.\n- [x] Gerrit submits the release change and the resulting commit is on main.\n- [x] release.yml is dispatched from main with version input 0.13.1.\n- [x] The required pypi environment deployment is approved.\n- [x] Every required release.yml job completes successfully (build, wheel_test, sdist_test,\n      publish, mcp_verify, mcp_registry, github_release).\n- [x] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.13.1.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The pypi-attestations verifier passes against the published 0.13.1\n      wheel scoped to the navapbc/rebar repository.\n      provenance: environment=local-macos-shell; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — downloaded the published wheel from files.pythonhosted.org and ran `pypi-attestations verify pypi nava_rebar-0.13.1-py3-none-any.whl --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar`, which printed \"OK: nava_rebar-0.13.1-py3-none-any.whl\".\n- [x] [non-codebase] GitHub tag v0.13.1 resolves to the released main commit.\n      provenance: environment=local-macos-shell; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — `gh release view v0.13.1 --repo navapbc/rebar` returned tagName=v0.13.1, publishedAt=2026-08-30T03:33:58Z, targeting the commit created by the release.yml github_release job off main.\n- [x] [non-codebase] GitHub Release v0.13.1 is marked Latest and attaches the 0.13.1 wheel\n      and sdist.\n      provenance: environment=local-macos-shell; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — `gh release list --repo navapbc/rebar` shows v0.13.1 flagged \"Latest\"; release.yml's github_release job (which attaches the build-once wheel/sdist) completed successfully in run 33290369748.\n- [x] [non-codebase, known-blocked-risk] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar\n      version 0.13.1 as isLatest, or (if blocked by the known OAuth-App restriction even\n      after the mitigation above) a linked follow-up ticket documents the gap and this item\n      is explicitly marked as the accepted exception.\n      provenance: environment=local-macos-shell; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — GET https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/v0/servers?search=rebar shows the io.github.navapbc/rebar entry at version=0.13.1 with isLatest=true, status=active (no exception needed; the mcp_registry job in release.yml run 33290369748 succeeded, unlike the 0.13.0 release).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.13.1 PyPI sdist URL with\n      matching SHA-256 (or the scheduled autobump run is confirmed to have picked it up).\n      provenance: environment=local-macos-shell; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — manually dispatched navapbc/homebrew-rebar's \"Autobump formula from PyPI\" workflow (run 33290636554, success) since the scheduled poll predated the publish; confirmed via `gh api repos/navapbc/homebrew-rebar/contents/Formula/rebar.rb` that the formula's url/sha256 now reference nava_rebar-0.13.1.tar.gz and its matching PyPI-reported sha256.\n- [x] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with\n      zero failures.\n- [x] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this\n      ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788061612350880001,"uuid":"2c050875-356d-423c-a0ee-59fcba0860ab"}